-- Schema 3 -> 4: the record-export tally.
--
-- The free plan gains an allowance of record PDF exports rather than being refused them
-- outright, so something has to count the ones already taken. Nothing existing could: unlike a
-- detected fill, which leaves a `fuel_fills` row that says how it arrived, an export leaves no
-- trace at all once the file is handed to the share sheet.
--
-- Device-local and unsynced, matching `scan_usage`. See RecordExportUsage.sq for why, and for
-- why the table is keyed by month while the cap in force is a lifetime one.
--
-- A plain CREATE TABLE: nothing is being altered, so there is no SQLite 3.18 rebuild to do
-- here. An install upgrading from 3 has no exports counted, which is correct — it also has no
-- cap until this release, so its owner starts the allowance whole rather than part-spent.
CREATE TABLE record_export_usage (
    month        TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    export_count INTEGER NOT NULL
);
